@startuml
' System-level context diagram for section 2.1.2.
' Authored in Slice 1. Renders through scripts/render-diagrams.sh.
!include style.puml
title Context diagram: the system and its environment

left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

actor "Store\nmanager" as SM
actor "DC\nmanager" as DM
node "External\nPOS system\n(one per store)" as POS #6FA8DC
node "External Analytics\nClient (future\nsubscriber)" as ANLY #6FA8DC

rectangle "**Supermarket Inventory Tracking System**" as SYS {
  rectangle "Store\n(3 today, up to 10)" as ST #93C47D
  rectangle "Distribution center" as DCB #F1C232
}

POS --> ST : one-way event stream:\nsales events
SM --> ST : inventory queries,\norder confirmation
ST --> DCB : inventory events, shipping orders\nover the WAN link [secure]\n
DM --> DCB : queries and reports
DCB --> ANLY : inventory events

legend bottom
  The outer box is our system boundary, so the WAN link between a store and the
  distribution center is inside it. Green is the store side; gold is the distribution
  center. Blue nodes are external systems; stick figures are human roles. Arrows show
  the information that crosses each connection.
endlegend
@enduml
